==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[mover]] [[and]] [[shaker]]|movers and shakers}}

# {{label|en|idiomatic}} Someone who has [[power]] and [[influence]] in a [[field]] or [[activity]]; one [[accomplish]]es tasks, who gets things done.
#: ''The sales team sought to talk to the '''movers and shakers''' within an organization, rather than to their underlings.''
#: ''He really is a '''mover and a shaker''' in those circles.''

====Usage notes====
* This term is often used in the plural.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|instigator}}, {{l|en|straw that stirs the drink}}

